1
00:00:05,315 --> 00:00:09,486
[HOLMES] MP Whiteley, murdered
by the Lord of Crime.

2
00:00:10,487 --> 00:00:13,115
[HOLMES]
There's more at play here.

3
00:00:19,204 --> 00:00:20,539
Yes, Miss Hudson?

4
00:00:20,581 --> 00:00:21,916
What's the matter?

5
00:00:21,957 --> 00:00:23,250
[HUDSON giggles]

6
00:00:25,168 --> 00:00:28,714
John? Who's this?

7
00:00:28,756 --> 00:00:31,717
May I present Miss Mary Morstan.

8
00:00:31,759 --> 00:00:34,052
Currently, she's employed
for Misses Forrester,

9
00:00:34,094 --> 00:00:35,888
serving as a governess.

10
00:00:37,139 --> 00:00:40,225
I'm a little late
in announcing this, but

11
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:43,103
you see, we're getting married.

12
00:00:44,688 --> 00:00:46,356
[HOLMES]
Uh.

13
00:02:17,489 --> 00:02:19,241
[HOLMES]
Misses Forrester, you said?

14
00:02:19,282 --> 00:02:21,869
The same one I consulted
two months ago?

15
00:02:21,911 --> 00:02:23,161
Right.

16
00:02:23,203 --> 00:02:25,664
After the case, she invited
the both of us to dinner.

17
00:02:25,706 --> 00:02:27,416
I was the only taker.

18
00:02:27,457 --> 00:02:30,377
Good thing. That was
where I met Mary.

19
00:02:30,419 --> 00:02:32,963
Yes. If I may be honest,

20
00:02:33,005 --> 00:02:34,840
Misses Forrester was
disappointed

21
00:02:34,882 --> 00:02:36,592
you weren't able to attend.

22
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:39,261
But she understands you
are a rather busy man.

23
00:02:39,302 --> 00:02:42,431
[WATSON] Even so, I'm
glad I didn't miss it.

24
00:02:42,472 --> 00:02:50,105
[WATSON] We might have
never run into each other.

25
00:02:50,146 --> 00:02:51,857
[HOLMES]
What else?

26
00:02:51,899 --> 00:02:53,525
Clearly there's another matter
besides your wedding

27
00:02:53,567 --> 00:02:55,485
that you came to bother me with.

28
00:02:55,527 --> 00:02:56,528
[GROUP grunts]

29
00:02:56,570 --> 00:02:58,363
How rude! Do you just blurt out

30
00:02:58,405 --> 00:02:59,448
whatever thought
enters your head?

31
00:02:59,489 --> 00:03:02,117
Come now, she's nervous
enough without you--

32
00:03:02,158 --> 00:03:04,411
[MARY]
John. [grunts]

33
00:03:04,453 --> 00:03:06,455
Mister Holmes is correct.

34
00:03:06,496 --> 00:03:07,873
[WATSON grunts]

35
00:03:07,915 --> 00:03:09,249
Now, however,

36
00:03:09,291 --> 00:03:13,670
I feel as though it'll sound
like a rather brazen request.

37
00:03:13,712 --> 00:03:15,672
Please proceed.

38
00:03:19,551 --> 00:03:22,345
[MARY] If you would
kindly have a look at these.

39
00:03:22,387 --> 00:03:26,016
Astounding! I've never laid eyes
on pearls as large as those!

40
00:03:26,058 --> 00:03:27,392
Judging from the size,

41
00:03:27,434 --> 00:03:30,729
you could live for half a year
by the sale of a single one.

42
00:03:30,771 --> 00:03:33,607
[MARY] These pearls started
arriving out of the blue,

43
00:03:33,649 --> 00:03:36,735
once per year, and each
one on the same day,

44
00:03:36,777 --> 00:03:38,737
starting about six years ago.

45
00:03:38,779 --> 00:03:42,741
The sender's name isn't
provided on the postage slip.

46
00:03:42,783 --> 00:03:45,535
Take me through
the order of events.

47
00:03:45,577 --> 00:03:47,830
Of course. But to do so,

48
00:03:47,871 --> 00:03:51,541
I must begin by telling you
all about my dearest father.

49
00:03:52,793 --> 00:03:54,169
[MARY]
He was a soldier.

50
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:56,546
An officer who
was posted to India.

51
00:03:56,588 --> 00:03:58,966
My mother passed away
when I was young,

52
00:03:59,008 --> 00:04:02,803
so I was taken in by a girls'
boarding school while he served.

53
00:04:02,845 --> 00:04:06,640
Then, ten years ago,
my father sent me a telegram.

54
00:04:06,682 --> 00:04:10,477
He was home on leave and
asked me to come to his hotel.

55
00:04:10,519 --> 00:04:13,147
I was excited to
see his face again,

56
00:04:13,188 --> 00:04:15,273
but when I arrived,

57
00:04:15,315 --> 00:04:16,566
his room--

58
00:04:16,608 --> 00:04:21,321
It was completely empty
save for his luggage.

59
00:04:21,363 --> 00:04:24,240
And to this day, I'm afraid
that his whereabouts

60
00:04:24,282 --> 00:04:27,410
remain a complete mystery to me.

61
00:04:27,452 --> 00:04:30,164
His disappearance and
the arrival of the pearls.

62
00:04:30,205 --> 00:04:32,833
What do you believe
is their connection?

63
00:04:32,875 --> 00:04:34,209
Not very long ago,

64
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:37,629
I learned about my
father's time during the war.

65
00:04:37,671 --> 00:04:39,173
While stationed in India,

66
00:04:39,214 --> 00:04:43,093
he became close to a Major
Sholto from his regiment .

67
00:04:43,135 --> 00:04:45,846
I thought perhaps he
might know something,

68
00:04:45,888 --> 00:04:48,264
but after looking
up his address,

69
00:04:48,306 --> 00:04:52,435
I learnt that he had passed away
six years ago, unfortunately.

70
00:04:52,477 --> 00:04:53,812
I see.

71
00:04:53,854 --> 00:04:55,856
Right around the same
time these pearls

72
00:04:55,898 --> 00:04:58,067
first began
arriving in the mail.

73
00:04:58,108 --> 00:05:01,070
Which is why you believe
the two events are related.

74
00:05:01,111 --> 00:05:02,779
[MARY]
Mm.

75
00:05:02,821 --> 00:05:05,574
Mister Holmes, I beg of you.

76
00:05:05,615 --> 00:05:09,369
I wish to know what
has become of my father.

77
00:05:09,411 --> 00:05:12,915
Would you please lend
me your assistance?

78
00:05:12,956 --> 00:05:16,418
[HOLMES] I will give it
my undivided attention.

79
00:05:18,170 --> 00:05:19,546
Do forgive me, John.

80
00:05:19,588 --> 00:05:22,758
I didn't mean to spring
this on you so suddenly.

81
00:05:22,799 --> 00:05:24,051
No worries.

82
00:05:24,093 --> 00:05:28,346
Rest assured, Sherlock and I
will unravel this mystery.

83
00:05:28,388 --> 00:05:30,057
Thank you, John.

84
00:05:34,686 --> 00:05:37,647
Miss Morstan--what
a charming young lady.

85
00:05:37,689 --> 00:05:40,567
[HOLMES] You think so?
I didn't particularly notice.

86
00:05:40,609 --> 00:05:42,694
[HUDSON gasps]
You're joking.

87
00:05:42,736 --> 00:05:44,113
You mean the master of detection

88
00:05:44,154 --> 00:05:46,698
couldn't see what was right
in front of his nose?

89
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,617
[HOLMES] To be fair,
she wasn't forthright.

90
00:05:48,658 --> 00:05:51,120
[gasps]

91
00:05:51,161 --> 00:05:52,454
I don't know what it is yet,

92
00:05:52,495 --> 00:05:54,998
but she's holding
something back.

93
00:05:57,793 --> 00:06:00,170
[MARY]
Pondicherry Lodge?

94
00:06:00,212 --> 00:06:01,797
Major Sholto's estate.

95
00:06:01,838 --> 00:06:04,258
A vast property
purchased 11 years ago

96
00:06:04,299 --> 00:06:07,010
after completing his
service in India.

97
00:06:07,052 --> 00:06:08,720
Apparently, he retired.

98
00:06:08,762 --> 00:06:11,223
Thanks to his business
dealings overseas,

99
00:06:11,265 --> 00:06:12,849
the major returned a rich man

100
00:06:12,891 --> 00:06:16,228
along with a menagerie
of rare curosities.

101
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:18,354
But no matter how
hard I searched,

102
00:06:18,396 --> 00:06:22,400
I wasn't able to find any record
of him doing business in India.

103
00:06:22,442 --> 00:06:26,113
Once home, it's said he lived
an extravagant lifestyle,

104
00:06:26,155 --> 00:06:28,531
But strangely,
became deathly afraid

105
00:06:28,573 --> 00:06:30,408
of going out in public alone.

106
00:06:30,450 --> 00:06:32,035
[gun fires]

107
00:06:33,287 --> 00:06:35,580
[HOLMES] Also of note,
there was an incident

108
00:06:35,622 --> 00:06:38,292
where he mistakenly fired
a gun at a merchant,

109
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:40,418
a man with a wooden leg.

110
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:43,297
But why on earth
would he do that?

111
00:06:52,264 --> 00:06:53,849
That's odd.

112
00:07:04,776 --> 00:07:06,320
[gasps]

113
00:07:08,030 --> 00:07:09,781
[HOLMES]
John! Quickly!

114
00:07:12,617 --> 00:07:15,078
[WATSON panting] What the
devil is it, Sherlock?

115
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,746
We're intruding!

116
00:07:17,747 --> 00:07:20,167
[HOLMES]
You in there! Are you all right?

117
00:07:20,209 --> 00:07:23,212
Damn!

118
00:07:23,253 --> 00:07:24,963
[HOLMES gasps]

119
00:07:27,966 --> 00:07:30,260
What? My word!

120
00:07:32,179 --> 00:07:35,932
[HOLMES] This is finally
shaping up to be a case.

121
00:07:43,857 --> 00:07:46,318
[WATSON]
He's dead. Who is he?

122
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,945
He's one of Major
Sholto's twin sons.

123
00:07:48,987 --> 00:07:51,781
Either Thaddeus or Bartholomew.

124
00:07:59,873 --> 00:08:03,459
[HOLMES] Cleary a victim of
homicide. Have a look, John.

125
00:08:03,501 --> 00:08:07,047
[WATSON gasps] What is that?
Looks like a thorn.

126
00:08:07,089 --> 00:08:11,301
A poison barb, it seems.
Definitely not from England.

127
00:08:19,601 --> 00:08:21,561
[HOLMES sniffs]

128
00:08:26,983 --> 00:08:28,944
[MARY yelps]

129
00:08:31,029 --> 00:08:31,947
[THADDEUS]
Who's there?

130
00:08:31,988 --> 00:08:33,656
[gasps]

131
00:08:33,698 --> 00:08:36,285
No, it can't be. Are you...

132
00:08:36,326 --> 00:08:37,911
...Miss Mary Morstan?

133
00:08:37,953 --> 00:08:39,246
[gasps]

134
00:08:40,163 --> 00:08:42,916
[THADDEUS] But what are
you doing in our mansion?

135
00:08:42,958 --> 00:08:44,667
[THADDEUS gasping]

136
00:08:44,709 --> 00:08:46,544
[THADDEUS]
Bartholomew!

137
00:08:46,586 --> 00:08:51,133
[gasps] My dear brother!
What's happened to you?

138
00:08:51,174 --> 00:08:52,926
[HOLMES]
You must be the other twin.

139
00:08:52,968 --> 00:08:54,719
Thaddeus, right?

140
00:08:54,761 --> 00:08:57,013
I need you to shed
light on a few matters:

141
00:08:57,055 --> 00:08:58,848
Where Mary's father is,

142
00:08:58,890 --> 00:09:00,850
the pearls that are
being sent to her,

143
00:09:00,892 --> 00:09:02,477
as well as your brother's death.

144
00:09:02,518 --> 00:09:03,853
[THADDEUS grunts]

145
00:09:03,895 --> 00:09:05,480
[gun fires]

146
00:09:05,521 --> 00:09:06,898
[THADDEUS]
After the shooting incident,

147
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:09,776
my father rarely
ventured in public again.

148
00:09:09,818 --> 00:09:11,820
Then six years ago,

149
00:09:11,861 --> 00:09:14,489
outside, drawn on
the mansion's gate

150
00:09:14,530 --> 00:09:16,992
were four mysterious symbols.

151
00:09:17,033 --> 00:09:19,577
My father nearly collapsed.

152
00:09:19,619 --> 00:09:21,746
Afterward, he became bedridden,

153
00:09:21,788 --> 00:09:24,624
and finally told us
his confession.

154
00:09:24,666 --> 00:09:27,002
Oh, my word.

155
00:09:27,043 --> 00:09:29,004
[SHOLTO]
The Treasure of Agra.

156
00:09:29,045 --> 00:09:32,507
Or to be more precise,
one small piece of it.

157
00:09:32,548 --> 00:09:36,052
See, I did not obtain my fortune
through business ventures.

158
00:09:36,094 --> 00:09:37,637
It was sheer luck.

159
00:09:37,679 --> 00:09:42,184
My subordinate Morstan and I
came upon it quite unexpectedly.

160
00:09:42,225 --> 00:09:44,602
I resigned my post immediately

161
00:09:44,644 --> 00:09:47,230
and brought the treasure
back to England.

162
00:09:47,272 --> 00:09:49,149
It was about a year later,

163
00:09:49,191 --> 00:09:52,694
Morstan also returned
and arrived at my door.

164
00:09:52,735 --> 00:09:57,282
However, the reunion was short
lived, a quarrel broke out.

165
00:09:57,324 --> 00:09:59,993
How we should
divide the treasure.

166
00:10:00,035 --> 00:10:02,496
[inaudible]

167
00:10:02,537 --> 00:10:04,622
[SHOLTO]
Whereupon...

168
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:12,047
If only I had called a doctor,
my comrade may have survived.

169
00:10:12,088 --> 00:10:14,383
Alas.

170
00:10:14,424 --> 00:10:17,135
Promise me, you will give
what remains of the treasure

171
00:10:17,177 --> 00:10:19,429
to Morstan's only daughter,
Mary.

172
00:10:19,471 --> 00:10:22,724
You'll find it hidden
in the mansion's--

173
00:10:22,765 --> 00:10:25,101
[screaming]

174
00:10:25,143 --> 00:10:27,812
[SHOLTO]
I-It's him! He's come for me!

175
00:10:27,854 --> 00:10:28,771
Drive that fiend away at once!

176
00:10:28,813 --> 00:10:30,857
[THADDEUS]
I dashed over to the window.

177
00:10:30,899 --> 00:10:33,360
But there was no one there.

178
00:10:33,402 --> 00:10:35,070
When I turned around,

179
00:10:35,111 --> 00:10:38,532
my father had already
taken his last breath.

180
00:10:38,573 --> 00:10:39,991
After his passing,

181
00:10:40,033 --> 00:10:42,452
my brother and I
searched for the treasure.

182
00:10:42,494 --> 00:10:44,579
But to no avail.

183
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:47,582
So I started sending her
whatever I could,

184
00:10:47,623 --> 00:10:50,460
one pearl each year.

185
00:10:50,502 --> 00:10:52,712
So that's what happened.

186
00:10:52,754 --> 00:10:56,132
I'm sorry, Mary, truly.

187
00:10:57,675 --> 00:10:59,635
So it exists after all.

188
00:10:59,677 --> 00:11:00,554
[HOLMES]
Hm?

189
00:11:00,595 --> 00:11:02,972
The Treasure of Agra.

190
00:11:05,683 --> 00:11:07,352
We believed it to be lost.

191
00:11:07,394 --> 00:11:10,146
Then my brother discovered
the chest just the other day.

192
00:11:10,188 --> 00:11:12,524
How did everything go so wrong?

193
00:11:12,566 --> 00:11:16,652
After our father passed,
we found this in the safe.

194
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:21,533
[HOLMES] The paper is Indian
and displays some sort of map,

195
00:11:21,575 --> 00:11:24,494
accompanied by a row
of four blood seals.

196
00:11:24,536 --> 00:11:31,626
Jonathan Small, Abdullah Tonga,
John Sholto, and Arthur Morstan.

197
00:11:31,667 --> 00:11:33,587
Small and Tonga--who are they?

198
00:11:33,628 --> 00:11:35,671
[THADDEUS]
I do not know.

199
00:11:35,713 --> 00:11:37,215
Thaddeus.

200
00:11:37,257 --> 00:11:40,176
Go to the police and tell them
all that has transpired.

201
00:11:40,218 --> 00:11:42,178
Uh, right.

202
00:11:45,557 --> 00:11:48,977
Now then, if we proceed
beyond this point,

203
00:11:49,018 --> 00:11:50,770
there is no turning back.

204
00:11:50,812 --> 00:11:53,523
There's no turning back?
What do you mean?

205
00:11:53,565 --> 00:11:56,651
First Major Sholto was
terrified of someone.

206
00:11:56,692 --> 00:12:00,196
Then, his son,
Bartholomew, is murdered.

207
00:12:00,238 --> 00:12:02,282
The evidence
indicates another party

208
00:12:02,324 --> 00:12:04,075
interested in the treasure.

209
00:12:04,117 --> 00:12:07,912
Someone who will go to
any lengths to obtain it.

210
00:12:07,954 --> 00:12:11,958
From here on out, we cannot
guarantee Miss Morstan's safety.

211
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,794
I believe now's the time
for us to withdraw.

212
00:12:14,836 --> 00:12:16,754
Not to mention
our original design

213
00:12:16,796 --> 00:12:18,465
was never to
obtain the treasure.

214
00:12:18,507 --> 00:12:19,715
[MARY grunts]

215
00:12:19,757 --> 00:12:22,677
You're right. I refuse to
expose Mary to any danger.

216
00:12:22,718 --> 00:12:24,554
While I'm curious
who the culprit is,

217
00:12:24,596 --> 00:12:27,932
we have learnt about her
father's fate and the treasure.

218
00:12:27,974 --> 00:12:31,727
Let the police handle the rest.
We should return home.

219
00:12:36,441 --> 00:12:39,528
[MARY gulps]
We can't.

220
00:12:39,569 --> 00:12:40,736
We must go on.

221
00:12:40,778 --> 00:12:42,113
Given the current situation,

222
00:12:42,155 --> 00:12:44,491
I am convinced suspicion
of Bartholomew's murder

223
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:47,118
will fall upon either
ourselves or Thaddeus.

224
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:48,411
[WATSON gasps]

225
00:12:48,453 --> 00:12:51,122
[MARY] Not only did we
break into the mansion,

226
00:12:51,164 --> 00:12:53,875
but the door to this
room was also locked.

227
00:12:53,916 --> 00:12:56,294
We are the only ones
who can provide an alibi

228
00:12:56,336 --> 00:12:58,672
for each other if
the police suspect us.

229
00:12:58,713 --> 00:13:00,256
If we escape scrutiny,

230
00:13:00,298 --> 00:13:03,718
no doubt Thaddeus will become
the primary suspect instead.

231
00:13:03,759 --> 00:13:04,719
For his sake and our own,

232
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:08,014
I think we should
find the real culprit.

233
00:13:08,056 --> 00:13:09,724
[HOLMES]
And there we have it.

234
00:13:09,765 --> 00:13:12,810
On the surface, she wishes
to lend a helping hand,

235
00:13:12,852 --> 00:13:15,355
but is her true intent to
recover the stolen riches

236
00:13:15,397 --> 00:13:17,732
in the course of
catching the culprit?

237
00:13:17,773 --> 00:13:20,860
From the very start, Mary's
objective has been the treasure.

238
00:13:20,902 --> 00:13:24,989
To be more precise, a fortune
purloined during war.

239
00:13:25,031 --> 00:13:28,117
It's possible she already
has plans how to spend it.

240
00:13:28,159 --> 00:13:29,411
If that's the case,

241
00:13:29,452 --> 00:13:31,162
it's extremely
likely she's involved

242
00:13:31,204 --> 00:13:33,707
in some manner of heinous crime.

243
00:13:33,748 --> 00:13:37,043
If she attempts to conceal it
before marrying John,

244
00:13:37,085 --> 00:13:39,754
I'll have no choice,
but to expose her,

245
00:13:39,795 --> 00:13:41,839
and reveal the truth...

246
00:13:41,881 --> 00:13:43,841
...for John's sake.

247
00:13:45,176 --> 00:13:48,555
So, in other words, all that's
needed is proving a third party

248
00:13:48,597 --> 00:13:51,349
was in this room
before any of us.

249
00:13:51,391 --> 00:13:52,308
Bob's your uncle.

250
00:13:52,350 --> 00:13:53,268
[BOTH gasp]

251
00:13:53,309 --> 00:13:54,852
First, Bartholomew was killed by

252
00:13:54,894 --> 00:13:57,772
a pair of criminals
working together.

253
00:13:57,813 --> 00:14:00,858
Earlier, I observed the ground
directly beneath the room.

254
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:02,110
One set of footprints

255
00:14:02,151 --> 00:14:05,029
had a circular indentation
that was rather distinct.

256
00:14:05,071 --> 00:14:09,534
Made from a wooden leg, no
doubt. Sholto's tormentor.

257
00:14:09,576 --> 00:14:11,786
Then, there's the
windowsill mark

258
00:14:11,827 --> 00:14:15,290
from where a rope
rubbed the ledge.

259
00:14:15,331 --> 00:14:17,709
Judging by the footprints
left in the room,

260
00:14:17,751 --> 00:14:21,254
the second man was smaller,
light on his feet.

261
00:14:21,296 --> 00:14:25,091
He would've been able to clamber
up to the window and slip in,

262
00:14:25,133 --> 00:14:28,094
then lower the chest from
the room to the ground below

263
00:14:28,136 --> 00:14:30,930
where the one-legged
man was waiting.

264
00:14:32,348 --> 00:14:34,434
Based on all the evidence,

265
00:14:34,476 --> 00:14:37,937
it's very clear someone
else was responsible.

266
00:14:37,979 --> 00:14:40,315
Is there a chance the culprits
are Small and Tonga--

267
00:14:40,356 --> 00:14:42,651
the remaining pair of
the four signatories?

268
00:14:42,692 --> 00:14:44,026
Do you know them?

269
00:14:44,068 --> 00:14:45,654
[MARY] My father was
the officer in command

270
00:14:45,695 --> 00:14:48,030
of a local battalion in India.

271
00:14:48,072 --> 00:14:50,659
If I had to surmise,

272
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:54,579
Small and Tonga most likely
both served under his command.

273
00:14:54,621 --> 00:14:57,999
Those blood seals may have
been forged as a contract.

274
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:00,876
[WATSON] Meaning Major Sholto
feared they would take revenge--

275
00:15:00,918 --> 00:15:03,921
retaliation for keeping
the treasure all to himself.

276
00:15:03,963 --> 00:15:05,131
[MARY]
Mister Holmes,

277
00:15:05,173 --> 00:15:07,509
how do we go about
finding these villains?

278
00:15:07,550 --> 00:15:09,177
That's remarkably simple.

279
00:15:09,218 --> 00:15:10,470
[WATSON, MARY grunt]

280
00:15:10,512 --> 00:15:13,097
[HOLMES] When the smaller
man was lowering the chest,

281
00:15:13,139 --> 00:15:16,726
he accidentally broke
a bottle of creosol.

282
00:15:16,768 --> 00:15:20,855
A powerful scent that
does not easily wash out.

283
00:15:21,939 --> 00:15:24,484
[HOLMES]
The expert has arrived.

284
00:15:24,526 --> 00:15:26,736
With his amazing power of scent,

285
00:15:26,778 --> 00:15:31,032
he's served as a consultant
on many a case, Toby.

286
00:15:31,073 --> 00:15:33,451
Well done, came
through in a pinch.

287
00:15:33,493 --> 00:15:34,661
You could make it up to me.

288
00:15:34,703 --> 00:15:39,248
An after-hours bonus
plus one if he finds your man.

289
00:15:39,290 --> 00:15:41,501
Are you having a laugh?

290
00:15:41,543 --> 00:15:43,878
Mary, dear. Would you
take the carriage Wiggins

291
00:15:43,919 --> 00:15:47,173
brought with him and
wait for us at Baker Street?

292
00:15:47,215 --> 00:15:48,675
Please do.

293
00:15:48,717 --> 00:15:49,759
Tracking down the culprits

294
00:15:49,801 --> 00:15:53,471
and the treasure is
a task best left to us.

295
00:15:53,513 --> 00:15:54,972
I'll do as you ask,

296
00:15:55,014 --> 00:15:56,974
but promise me
you'll be careful.

297
00:15:57,016 --> 00:15:58,267
[WATSON]
Mm.

298
00:15:58,309 --> 00:16:00,102
Right then, the hunt is on!

299
00:16:00,144 --> 00:16:01,604
Toby, come along!

300
00:16:01,646 --> 00:16:02,689
[TOBY barks]

301
00:16:02,731 --> 00:16:04,106
[MARY grunts]

302
00:16:12,990 --> 00:16:14,492
[WATSON]
I made some coffee.

303
00:16:14,534 --> 00:16:15,910
Care for some?

304
00:16:15,951 --> 00:16:17,245
Gladly, thanks.

305
00:16:17,286 --> 00:16:19,706
Seen any activity
on the boat yet?

306
00:16:19,748 --> 00:16:21,916
[HOLMES] The coffee isn't
the only thing steaming.

307
00:16:21,957 --> 00:16:23,959
They're preparing to launch.

308
00:16:24,001 --> 00:16:28,506
Small should be arriving soon.
He's bound to make his escape.

309
00:16:28,548 --> 00:16:31,551
And when he does,
we'll pursue and capture him.

310
00:16:31,593 --> 00:16:33,928
Why go through the trouble
of chasing the boat?

311
00:16:33,969 --> 00:16:35,764
We could easily end
this by arresting them

312
00:16:35,805 --> 00:16:37,223
before they depart.

313
00:16:37,265 --> 00:16:39,975
We wouldn't be able to
keep Mary safe if we did.

314
00:16:40,017 --> 00:16:42,228
[WATSON grunts]
What do you mean?

315
00:16:42,270 --> 00:16:44,814
Small may not have
murdered Bartholomew,

316
00:16:44,856 --> 00:16:49,360
but the burglary may prove
to be a rather unique challenge.

317
00:16:49,402 --> 00:16:51,780
After getting out of
jail in a few years,

318
00:16:51,821 --> 00:16:54,156
if the treasure is
in Mary's possession,

319
00:16:54,198 --> 00:16:56,743
he will surely come
to claim it from her.

320
00:16:56,785 --> 00:16:58,077
[gasps]

321
00:16:58,119 --> 00:17:01,080
There's one way for us to
prevent any future reprisals.

322
00:17:01,122 --> 00:17:06,127
We need Small to abandon all
claim he has to the treasure.

323
00:17:06,168 --> 00:17:07,462
How can we force him to--

324
00:17:07,503 --> 00:17:12,091
[engine sputters]

325
00:17:12,133 --> 00:17:13,676
[HOLMES]
Speak of the devil!

326
00:17:13,718 --> 00:17:15,511
Wooden-leg, 12 o' clock.

327
00:17:15,553 --> 00:17:18,765
May I present, Small!

328
00:17:18,807 --> 00:17:19,849
Look alive, you lot!

329
00:17:19,891 --> 00:17:22,059
Lestrade! Get after that launch!

330
00:17:22,101 --> 00:17:23,311
And you're absolutely certain

331
00:17:23,352 --> 00:17:25,647
there's a murderer
aboard the boat, right?

332
00:17:25,688 --> 00:17:27,440
[HOLMES]
For the thousandth time, yes!

333
00:17:27,482 --> 00:17:28,566
Hurry!

334
00:17:28,608 --> 00:17:30,485
Douse the lights so
they don't see us coming!

335
00:17:30,526 --> 00:17:32,445
By Jove, put yourself
in my shoes--

336
00:17:32,487 --> 00:17:35,281
taking a Yard police-boat
without permission like this!

337
00:17:35,323 --> 00:17:37,533
C'mon, get us moving!

338
00:17:47,251 --> 00:17:49,629
[WATSON]
Distance, about 50 yards.

339
00:17:49,671 --> 00:17:50,839
[HOLMES]
All right.

340
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:54,258
This should be plenty deep
enough. Hit the lights!

341
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:55,050
Huh?

342
00:17:55,092 --> 00:17:57,094
[HOLMES]
Ahoy, Jonathan Small!

343
00:17:57,136 --> 00:17:59,096
Abdullah Tonga!

344
00:17:59,138 --> 00:18:02,183
We're well aware of your
nefarious deeds, sirs!

345
00:18:02,224 --> 00:18:04,101
Hand over the Treasure of Agra,

346
00:18:04,143 --> 00:18:06,896
and answer for
killing Bartholomew!

347
00:18:06,938 --> 00:18:08,022
But how?

348
00:18:08,063 --> 00:18:10,149
We didn't leave a single
bloody witness behind.

349
00:18:10,191 --> 00:18:11,484
[CAPTAIN 21A gasps]

350
00:18:11,526 --> 00:18:13,820
I knew there was something
crooked about you two blokes!

351
00:18:13,862 --> 00:18:16,322
Watch your tongue!
I paid you a tidy sum!

352
00:18:16,364 --> 00:18:17,824
You're an accomplice now!

353
00:18:17,866 --> 00:18:19,325
So if you wish to
keep breathin',

354
00:18:19,367 --> 00:18:20,660
I suggest you lose 'em.

355
00:18:20,702 --> 00:18:21,870
[CAPTAIN 21A whimpers]

356
00:18:21,911 --> 00:18:23,496
[HOLMES] Stop the boat
and hand over the treasure,

357
00:18:23,538 --> 00:18:24,831
nice and easy!

358
00:18:24,873 --> 00:18:26,624
Fool! Don't be so dumb!

359
00:18:26,666 --> 00:18:29,836
A pact was made!
The treasure is rightfully ours!

360
00:18:31,253 --> 00:18:32,171
[SMALL, CAPTAIN 21A gasp]

361
00:18:32,213 --> 00:18:33,422
[WATSON]
Sherlock!

362
00:18:33,464 --> 00:18:35,967
[HOLMES] Stop the boat
if you want to live!

363
00:18:36,009 --> 00:18:36,885
He's mad!

364
00:18:36,926 --> 00:18:38,720
The thief means
to take our fortune,

365
00:18:38,761 --> 00:18:41,180
even if it requires shooting us!

366
00:18:44,099 --> 00:18:45,935
What are you doing?

367
00:18:45,977 --> 00:18:46,895
[WATSON gasps]

368
00:18:46,936 --> 00:18:48,563
[WATSON]
Sherlock! Watch out!

369
00:18:51,566 --> 00:18:52,149
[gun firing]

370
00:18:52,191 --> 00:18:53,359
[groans]

371
00:18:53,401 --> 00:18:55,653
They shot him!
It's all gone to hell!

372
00:18:55,695 --> 00:18:58,197
Captain! Can't this
rubbish heap move faster?!

373
00:18:58,239 --> 00:19:02,201
I already pushed her too hard!
The boiler is going to explode!

374
00:19:02,243 --> 00:19:04,453
[SMALL]
No. Damn it.

375
00:19:04,495 --> 00:19:06,372
Damn it all!

376
00:19:06,414 --> 00:19:09,042
It's not yours! The treasure,

377
00:19:09,083 --> 00:19:11,377
it's mine! All mine!

378
00:19:11,419 --> 00:19:13,337
You won't take it!

379
00:19:13,379 --> 00:19:16,591
I won't let you!

380
00:19:16,632 --> 00:19:20,595
No one's getting their
hands on what belongs to me!

381
00:19:20,636 --> 00:19:22,221
[thud]

382
00:19:22,263 --> 00:19:23,431
[HOLMES, WATSON gasp]

383
00:19:23,472 --> 00:19:27,351
[SMALL cackling]

384
00:19:27,393 --> 00:19:29,395
If you blokes still
want my treasure,

385
00:19:29,437 --> 00:19:31,689
it belongs to the Thames now.

386
00:19:31,731 --> 00:19:35,693
[SMALL cackling]

387
00:19:35,735 --> 00:19:37,695
[WATSON]
Huh. That's how...

388
00:19:37,737 --> 00:19:39,072
[HOLMES]
Indeed.

389
00:19:39,113 --> 00:19:40,990
Thanks to this spectacle,

390
00:19:41,032 --> 00:19:45,202
Small has voluntarily given up
his claim to the fortune.

391
00:19:45,244 --> 00:19:50,541
[SMALL cackling]

392
00:19:57,214 --> 00:20:00,093
On the whole, Small's
testimony was nearly identical

393
00:20:00,134 --> 00:20:02,804
to what you and
Sherlock deduced.

394
00:20:02,845 --> 00:20:04,305
[MARY] I'm relieved you
caught the criminals

395
00:20:04,346 --> 00:20:05,974
without incident.

396
00:20:07,475 --> 00:20:10,728
[MARY]
So then, where's the treasure?

397
00:20:10,770 --> 00:20:13,272
[WATSON]
Mary, the thing of it is...

398
00:20:13,314 --> 00:20:15,900
I'm afraid it all
went overboard.

399
00:20:15,942 --> 00:20:17,276
[gasps]

400
00:20:17,318 --> 00:20:19,361
[HOLMES] Rather than having
it fall into another's hands,

401
00:20:19,403 --> 00:20:22,197
he let the Thames claim it.

402
00:20:22,239 --> 00:20:23,449
It... was lost?

403
00:20:23,491 --> 00:20:26,744
For the best. If you had it
in your possession then,

404
00:20:26,786 --> 00:20:30,539
those two scoundrels would
come after you, looking for it.

405
00:20:30,581 --> 00:20:35,210
We have each other; that's
the only treasure we need.

406
00:20:35,252 --> 00:20:38,255
[MARY]
But without it, he's going to...

407
00:20:39,214 --> 00:20:42,969
[HOLMES] I did detect a sort of
desperation in your behaviour.

408
00:20:43,011 --> 00:20:46,722
You wanted your
hands on that gold.

409
00:20:46,764 --> 00:20:48,724
When you heard about the
existence of the treasure

410
00:20:48,766 --> 00:20:52,394
from Thaddeus, you did not
seem overly surprised.

411
00:20:52,436 --> 00:20:56,149
Which means, you knew
about it beforehand,

412
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:59,110
but hid the fact from us.

413
00:20:59,152 --> 00:21:01,570
Even after a murder
had been committed,

414
00:21:01,612 --> 00:21:05,324
you put recovering the fortune
above your own personal safety.

415
00:21:05,366 --> 00:21:08,577
Which might strike some as odd,
seeing as you are employed

416
00:21:08,619 --> 00:21:11,956
and haven't sold any of the
pearls that were sent to you.

417
00:21:11,998 --> 00:21:16,544
That tells me, you are not short
or in desperate need of cash.

418
00:21:16,585 --> 00:21:20,673
Once that's excluded, then
only one possibility remains.

419
00:21:20,715 --> 00:21:21,841
Blackmail.

420
00:21:21,883 --> 00:21:23,843
[MARY gasps]

421
00:21:23,885 --> 00:21:24,969
Then, I'm right.

422
00:21:25,011 --> 00:21:26,762
[WATSON]
Now, just a moment!

423
00:21:26,804 --> 00:21:30,058
Is that true? Mary,
who would blackmail you?

424
00:21:30,099 --> 00:21:34,562
[MARY whimpers] If I didn't
turn over the treasure,

425
00:21:34,603 --> 00:21:37,690
he said I would pay.
That he'd break up our wedding.

426
00:21:37,732 --> 00:21:41,861
[WATSON grunts]
Tell me the name of this devil!

427
00:21:41,903 --> 00:21:44,405
Who would dare stoop
to such a vile act?

428
00:21:44,446 --> 00:21:46,782
Only one name comes to mind.

429
00:21:46,824 --> 00:21:49,702
The king of blackmailers,

430
00:21:49,744 --> 00:21:52,663
Charles Augustus Milverton.

431
00:21:52,705 --> 00:21:55,208
Evil personified.

432
00:23:32,721 --> 00:23:35,766
[WILLIAM] Next time on
Moriarty the Patriot  :

433
00:23:35,808 --> 00:23:37,643
"The Two Criminals."
